U='https://dot.ca.gov/-/media/dot-media/programs/design/documents/2025_stdspecs.pdf'
ED='2025'
S='Caltrans Standard Specifications, 2025, Sections 19-3 and 19-5 (read 2026-11-20)'
add('spec-ca-backfill-1','CA','California Caltrans structure backfill and compaction numbers (Sections 19-3, 19-5)',
"California (Caltrans 2025 Standard Specifications, Section 19 Earthwork). Structure backfill, which is what goes around culverts and drainage structures: layers no more than 0.67 foot (8 inches) thick before compacting; relative compaction at least 95 percent; at least 90 percent is allowed at overside drains, headwalls, endwalls, culvert wingwalls and similar spots with nothing under pavement (19-3.03E(1)). Ponding and jetting is allowed only where the backfill drains freely and the foundation will not soften, in layers up to 4 feet, never in the top 4 feet below finished grade, and with vibratory compaction added. Slurry cement backfill: at least 188 lb of cement per cubic yard, placed within 1 hour of mixing, and nothing placed over it for at least 4 hours (19-3.02E, 19-3.03F). Soil cement bedding: at least 282 lb of cement per cubic yard and an 8-hour wait (19-3.02F(3), 19-3.03H). Controlled low-strength material beside pipe: 6 inches clear each side for pipe 42 inches and smaller or 20 feet or less of cover, 1 foot for bigger or deeper (19-3.03I). Embankment (19-5): 95 percent for 0.5 foot below the grading plane and 2.5 feet below finished grade under the traveled way plus 3 feet each side; 90 percent elsewhere. Caltrans 'relative compaction' is by California Test 216/231, not Proctor. City and district jobs usually follow the Greenbook or the agency's own book instead.",S,U,ED)
S='Caltrans Standard Specifications, 2025, Section 61 Drainage Facilities (read 2026-11-20; sections 64-66 not read)'
add('spec-ca-drainage-1','CA','California Caltrans drainage pipe joints and leak tests (Section 61)',
"California (Caltrans 2025 Standard Specifications, Section 61, Drainage Facilities, general). Pipe materials have their own sections: plastic pipe Section 64, concrete pipe Section 65, corrugated metal pipe Section 66. Watertight joints are proven by holding a 10-foot head of water above the pipe crown for 10 minutes (61-2.01D(2)(b)). Field leak testing is done on culverts and drainage structures only where the plans show it (61-2.01D(3)(a)); the low-pressure air test is not used on drainage pipe over 30 inches (61-2.01D(3)(c)). Concrete backfill in pipe trenches is consolidated with high-frequency internal vibrators, and with rapid-strength concrete nothing goes on top until it reaches 500 psi (61-5.03). For plastic pipe in saturated clay, unsuitable material is removed at least 1/4 of the pipe diameter, and not less than 6 inches, each side of the pipe. Not confirmed here: Caltrans minimum cover for construction loads and plastic pipe deflection limits (Sections 64 to 66); read the section or the plans.",S,U,ED,'medium')

# (Oregon: the live library already has or-1..or-3 with these numbers; see b09 spec-or-bore-1 for what is new)
