ED='2025'
S='CDOT Standard Specifications for Road and Bridge Construction, 2025, Section 206 (read 2026-11-20)'
add('spec-co-backfill-1','CO','Colorado CDOT structure backfill and compaction (Section 206)',
"Colorado (CDOT 2025 Standard Specifications for Road and Bridge Construction, Section 206, Structure Excavation and Backfill). Structure backfill is Class 1 or Class 2, or Flow-Fill. Each layer of backfill is 6 inches or less. Both classes are compacted to at least 95 percent of maximum dry density, within plus or minus 2 percent of optimum moisture (soils with more than 35 percent passing the No. 200 sieve at 0 to 3 percent above optimum). Maximum density is by AASHTO T 180 for Class 1 and for A-1, A-2-4, A-2-5 and A-3 soils, and by AASHTO T 99 (as modified by CP 23) for other Class 2 materials (206.03). Flow-Fill is not compacted and goes in lifts of 3 feet or less unless the Engineer approves more; the next lift waits until the surface dents less than 3 inches with no visible water (ASTM D6024). Do not backfill against new concrete until it reaches 0.8 f'c. Bed course material is per 703.07 (206.02(b)).",S,U,ED)
S='CDOT Standard Specifications for Road and Bridge Construction, 2025, Sections 603 and 604 (read 2026-11-20)'
add('spec-co-pipe-1','CO','Colorado CDOT culverts and sewers: bedding, joints, 5 percent deflection, leak test (Sections 603, 604)',
"Colorado (CDOT 2025 Standard Specifications, Section 603, Culverts and Sewers). Bedding: a layer of loose structure backfill at least 3 inches thick (603.05). In new embankment, build the fill to at least 0.3 times the pipe outside diameter or rise before trenching for the pipe. Storm drain joints must be watertight; sanitary sewer concrete pipe uses rubber gaskets (603.07). Deflection of metal and plastic pipe: 5 percent maximum, measured 30 days or more after installation with a mandrel, laser profile or another approved method; replaced pipe is retested after another 30 days (603.10). Reinforced concrete pipe gets a visual inspection per AASHTO LRFD Section 27.6. Sanitary sewer leak limit: no more than 0.6 gallon per inch of inside diameter per 100 feet per hour (603.09). Jacked pipe: no trenching; grout the outside with 1 part portland cement to 3 parts fine aggregate. Section 604, manholes and inlets: a manhole in pavement is not built to final grade until the paving is done; pay depth is in 5-foot steps (0 to 5.0 ft pays as 5, 5.1 to 10.0 as 10).",S,U,ED)
